.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt QCOM_ADSP 4 aarch64
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm qcom_adsp
.Nd "Qualcomm audio DSP loader"
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To compile this driver into the kernel,
place the following lines in your
kernel configuration file:
.Bd -ragged -offset indent
.Cd "device qcom_scm"
.Cd "device qcom_adsp"
.Ed
.Pp
Alternatively, to load the driver as a
module at boot time, place the following line in
.Xr loader.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
qcom_adsp_load="YES"
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver starts the audio DSP (ADSP) of Qualcomm Snapdragon systems-on-chip
with its board's firmware.
It loads the firmware into the memory reserved for the ADSP, and has the
TrustZone firmware authenticate it and start the ADSP through
.Xr qcom_scm 4 .
The firmware is read once the root file system is mounted, from a
.Xr firmware 9
module named after the file's path in linux-firmware with
.Ql / ,
.Ql \&.
and
.Ql -
turned into
.Ql _ ,
or from
.Pa /boot/firmware .
.Pp
The firmware is specific to each board, which the driver recognizes by its
SMBIOS system maker and product.
On the Radxa Dragon Q8B, the ADSP runs Radxa's fan control, which parks the
fan when the system is cool; without the ADSP the fan runs at full speed.
.Pp
The driver does not otherwise communicate with the ADSP, and cannot stop
it: it cannot be detached while the ADSP runs.
.Sh HARDWARE
The
.Nm
driver attaches to the ACPI device with hardware ID
.Qq QCOM061B
on the following boards:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
Radxa Dragon Q8B (Qualcomm Snapdragon 8cx Gen 3, SC8280XP),
with firmware
.Pa qcom/sc8280xp/radxa/dragon-q8b/qcadsp8280.mbn .
.El
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va dev.qcom_adsp.%d.state
Whether the ADSP is waiting to start, starting, running or stopped, or
why it failed to start.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr qcom_scm 4 ,
.Xr qcom_tsens 4 ,
.Xr firmware 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
.Sh AUTHORS
The
.Nm
driver and this manual page were written by
.An James Kane .
